Unzip 5.1 - Atari ST/MegaST/STe/MegaSTe Executables
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This directory contains executables suitable for any 16-bit or 32-bit
Atari computer.  If you have a TT, Falcon030, or any 68020-, 68030-, or
68040-based accelerated ST, you might want to consider using the
executables in the 68020 directory.

Important: See the NOTE below for information about Atari ST support for
encrypted ZIP files!

You may freely distribute these executables as long as they are
accompanied by the documentation that came with them.  In fact, you
_should_ spread Unzip around as much as you can!

NOTE:  Due to a silly oversite on my part, these Unzip binaries do NOT
       support encrypted ZIP files.  Sorry.  The encryption code is not
       present, and the binaries will simply skip over the encrypted
       files in a ZIP archive.  If this is a problem, PLEASE send me
       email at the address below; I'll be working on the encryption code
       in the next couple of weeks, and uploading an encryption-aware
       set of binaries to an FTP server outside of the US as soon as
       I'm done and have it tested.  Again, sorry for the inconvenience.

Any problems, questions, or bug-reports that are Atari-specific should
go to me at the address below.  semprini is connected via UUCP, so don't
send huge ZIP files illustrating your problem; I'll let you know how to
get large files to me if necessary.

-Chris-
cherborth@semprini.waterloo-rdp.on.ca
